      "writtenOn": "2024-08-02T13:33:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I saw the comment earlier about `EXPAND` ensuring that bit depth is at least 8, but does `rust_png` support 16-bit PNGs?",
      "revId": "c7170f4cc6aa359c75c84a63c5bac5af4cf751ae",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98273c45_f167b09d",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-05T22:06:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question - thanks for explicitly asking about this aspect of the CL.  Let\u0027s discuss further in the GVC code review meeting.\n\nAdditional notes:\n\n* We should decide if we want to use [`png::Transformations::STRIP_16`](https://docs.rs/png/latest/png/struct.Transformations.html#associatedconstant.STRIP_16) (in the short-term?  in the long-term?):\n    - Pros: no need to worry about 16-bit PNGs at all.  (In top 500 websites 16-bit PNGs accounted for ~0.12% of all PNG images [in October 2024](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1CEgr4ttd2agOZi-MFOjqJGqfDVFUKDp-zKbrF-8Xwyk/edit?gid\u003d1170535878#gid\u003d1170535878).)\n    - Cons: maybe supporting 16-bits will result in a more complete/robust `SkPngRustCodec` implementation?\n* Some notes that are relevant if don\u0027t want to use `STRIP_16`:\n    - IIUC `srcFormat` parameter of `SkCodec`\u0027s constructor describes the format of input for `applyColorXform`, which is *not* necessarily the format of PNG crate\u0027s output (because of how we use `SkSwizzler` before doing color transforms).\n    - Decoded pixels are first transformed using `SkSwizzler` (supports 16 bits) and `skcms_Transform` (supports 16 bits in RGBA and BGRA pixel format, in LE or BE, but does *not* support G16 or GA1616).  It is unclear to me if lack of G16 or GA16 support is a *new* problem.  If `dstInfo` asks for GA1616 (it can, right?), then maybe we already have a problem before this CL?\n    \n* I also note that hard coding `bits_per_component\u003d8` in `FFI.rs` doesn\u0027t fail any `gfx_unittests`.  I am not sure if we should address this by adding relevant coverage to `ui/gfx/codec/png_codec_unittests.cc` VS by covering `SkPngRustCodec` by Skia\u0027s tests (which hopefully include 16-bit PNGs?).",
      "parentUuid": "6373feb2_e1063eb2",
      "revId": "c7170f4cc6aa359c75c84a63c5bac5af4cf751ae",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61640d84_effb90e2",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T13:32:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d definitely push for 16 bit support in the long-term. And I\u0027m hopeful that it\u0027s not too difficult to just add it now, rather than wait.\n\nThere actually aren\u0027t any G16 or GA1616 SkColorTypes, so I don\u0027t think we have an existing issue - clients that want 16-bit output from the codec basically have to ask for RGBA (16 bit or float).\n\nAs for test coverage... Yes. Skia has an image test corpus that appears to include ~every possible PNG variant. Those files are stored in CIPD, but if you\u0027re authenticated with gcloud, you can probably fetch them from a skia repo:\n\n```\nbin/fetch-sk\nbin/sk asset download skimage images\nls images/dm/*.png\n```",
      "parentUuid": "98273c45_f167b09d",
      "revId": "c7170f4cc6aa359c75c84a63c5bac5af4cf751ae",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0d007b1_71cdd0c5",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
